  "_name": "t80_gateway_doorstep_hold",
  "_desc": "Regression for the first-leg-loop fix (gateway_doorstep_hold). Three suburb nodes s1/s2/s3 (layer 2, fully meshed with each other so the OLD code had sibling next-hops to cascade to) all fire a cross-layer send to 'target' (layer 1) at the same instant (t=25000), inside gw's SECOND visit window (windows are [4000,10000], [24000,30000], ...; the sends wait for the 2nd so the senders have already learned gw bridges L1 during the 1st). Their RTSs to gw collide -> cts_timeout. OLD behaviour: each fans the copy out to a sibling (path_cascade / blind_alt) -> copies bounce among s1/s2/s3 (loop_duplicate) and self-contend, often giving up within seconds. NEW behaviour: gateway_doorstep_hold keeps the single copy, requeues it window-aware + jittered (burst-avoidance), and retries the SAME gateway across visit windows until gateway_send_giveup_ms (150 s). Verify: (1) gateway_hold_requeue fires (the hold path engaged -- this event does not exist without the fix); (2) all three cross-layer messages reach target (burst-avoidance got them all through, no loop). Observed with the fix: 16 holds, 3/3 delivered, 0 path_cascade, 0 loop_duplicate, 0 send_giveup.",
